# CODEOWNERS — current owners of paths in this repo (no ownership history here).
# Compatible with common Git hosts that read a root CODEOWNERS file.
# Last matching rule wins. Put the fallback first; put more specific paths below.
# Path sections below are grouped by directory — see rule 7 for the layout.
#
# Learn more (example host docs):
# https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1218598/code-owners-for-bitbucket
#
# Rules:
# 1. Global fallback — every path has an owner until a more specific rule matches.
#      * @alice
#
# 2. Directory ownership — one person/team owns a whole app or lib tree.
#      /apps/ng-x-boilerplate-web/ @alice
#      /libs/shared/data-access/ng-auth/ @alice
#
# 3. Version-folder ownership — only for shared libs that use per-version folders
#    under `…/src/lib/{version}/` (see "Versioning shared libs" in
#    docs/getting-started/library-types-and-their-relationship.md).
#    Use when different people own different versions (e.g. `v1` vs `v2`, or
#    `toggle-me-v1` vs `long-press-me-v1`). App-specific libs are not versioned
#    this way — own them at the lib/app directory (rule 2).
#      /libs/shared/ui/ng-directives/src/lib/toggle-me-v1/ @bob
#      /libs/shared/ui/ng-modal/src/lib/modal-network-v1/ @carol
#
# 4. Teams — prefer a stable team over individuals when a group owns an area.
#      /docs/ @my-org/docs-team
#    Reviewer assignment depends on the host (team as a unit, or a subset via
#    host-specific group strategies such as :all / :random(n)).
#
# 5. Own this file — ownership changes must be reviewable.
#      CODEOWNERS @alice
#
# 6. Keep this file up to date (who is responsible for the path *now*):
#    When to edit this file:
#    - You create a new app, lib, or shared version-folder → add a line for it
#      with the current owner.
#    - Maintenance of a path is intentionally handed to another person/team
#      (a planned handoff agreed with the current owner / Workspace Specialist).
#      That is NOT "person B edited one file in person A's lib" — editing or
#      reviewing code does not change ownership by itself.
#    When to commit the edit:
#    - In the same commit that adds the new path, or that records the handoff.
#      Do not defer CODEOWNERS to a later commit.
#    Handoff tip: optional short co-ownership (@old @new), then remove @old.
#    Do not leave old owners or "formerly …" notes here (Git history records
#    past owners).
#
# 7. Layout — where a new line goes:
#    Sections are grouped by directory. Within a section, order by owner first
#    (alphabetically), then by path, and leave one blank line between owners.
#    Sort paths with `/` ranked below every other character, so a directory
#    comes before longer sibling names — `ng-bases/` before `ng-bases-model/`,
#    `ng-b2c/` before `ng-b2c-e2e/`. (Plain ASCII sorting inverts both, because
#    `-` < `/`.) Co-owned lines (`@alice @bob`) form their own group, ordered
#    by the full owner list.
#      /libs/shared/ui/ng-alpha/ @alice
#      /libs/shared/ui/ng-beta/ @alice
#
#      /libs/shared/ui/ng-gamma/ @bob
#    This ordering is cosmetic EXCEPT for one case that is not: a parent path
#    must stay ABOVE any path nested under it, even when owner order would put
#    it lower. Last matching rule wins, so a parent listed after its child
#    silently takes the child's ownership.
#      /apps/ng-x-boilerplate-web/ @alice          (parent first)
#      /apps/ng-x-boilerplate-web/android/ @bob    (nested override below it)
#
# Also: docs/guidelines/best-practices.md (Mindset → Prioritize docs).


